Leo: Yes! They say you can try a real flight simulator there.
Mia: That sounds awesome. Do you think we are brave enough to join?
Leo: Of course. We only need to submit a short video about ourselves.
Mia: I''m a little nervous, but I really want to learn about astronomy.
Leo: Me too. My dream is to become an astronaut one day.
Mia: Then let''s apply together this weekend.
Leo: Great idea. We can help each other write the video.', '米娅问里奥有没有看到暑期太空营的广告;里奥说能体验真正的飞行模拟器;米娅觉得很棒,但担心他们是否够勇敢;里奥说只需提交一段自我介绍的短视频;米娅有点紧张但很想学天文学;里奥的梦想是当宇航员;两人决定周末一起申请、互相帮忙拍视频。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What can people try at the space camp?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A real flight simulator.","A fishing boat.","A racing car.","A cooking class."]},{"q":"What do they need to submit to join?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A long written exam.","A short video about themselves.","A doctor''s letter.","A photo of their school."]},{"q":"How does Mia feel about joining?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A little nervous but eager.","Completely bored.","Angry with Leo.","Too tired to care."]},{"q":"What is Leo''s dream?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To open a restaurant.","To become an astronaut one day.","To stop studying science.","To travel by ship only."]},{"q":"When do they decide to apply?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Next year.","Never.","This weekend.","In ten years."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');
His flight lasted less than two hours, but it changed history.
Millions of people were amazed that a human could orbit the Earth.
His courage opened the door for many astronauts who came after him.
Today we still remember him as a hero of space exploration.', '1961年,尤里·加加林成为首位进入太空的人;他的飞行不到两个小时,却改变了历史;数百万人惊叹于人类竟能绕地球飞行;他的勇气为后来的许多宇航员打开了大门;今天我们仍把他当作太空探索的英雄铭记。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Yuri Gagarin become in 1961?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The first teacher in space.","The first man on the Moon.","The first to build a rocket.","The first person to travel into space."]},{"q":"How long did his flight last?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Less than two hours.","A whole week.","Exactly one day.","Several months."]},{"q":"Why were millions of people amazed?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He flew an aeroplane.","A human could orbit the Earth.","He climbed a mountain.","He swam across a sea."]},{"q":"What did his courage do for others?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It ended all space travel.","It made people afraid.","It opened the door for later astronauts.","It closed the space programme."]},{"q":"How is Gagarin remembered today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["As an unknown traveller.","As a famous cook.","As a sports star.","As a hero of space exploration."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Astronaut: Even simple tasks become difficult without gravity.
Student: Really? Can you give me an example?
Astronaut: Yes. We have to strap ourselves down just to sleep safely.
Student: That sounds strange. How do you stay healthy up there?
Astronaut: We must exercise every day, or our muscles grow weak.
Student: What about eating? Is that difficult too?
Astronaut: A little. Salt and pepper come in liquid form, or they would float away.', '学生问宇航员在太空生活最难的是什么;宇航员说没有重力,连简单的事都变难;比如睡觉时得把自己绑住才安全;为保持健康必须每天锻炼,否则肌肉会变弱;吃东西也有点难,盐和胡椒做成液体,否则会漂走。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What becomes difficult without gravity?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Even simple daily tasks.","Only very hard tasks.","Nothing at all.","Just reading books."]},{"q":"What must astronauts do just to sleep safely?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Turn off the lights.","Strap themselves down.","Hold hands together.","Float near the door."]},{"q":"Why do astronauts exercise every day?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To win a sports prize.","Because they are bored.","So their muscles do not grow weak.","To stay warm at night."]},{"q":"How do salt and pepper come in space?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In huge dry bags.","Frozen into ice.","Mixed into bread.","In liquid form."]},{"q":"Why are they in liquid form?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Otherwise they would float away.","To make them taste better.","To save money.","Because they are heavier."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Trainees learn to stay calm in a flight simulator that feels completely real.
They also practise moving in special pools that copy zero gravity.
Self-discipline is just as important as physical strength.
Only those who never give up are ready for a real mission.', '成为宇航员需要多年的艰苦训练;学员在逼真的飞行模拟器里学会保持冷静;他们还在模拟零重力的特殊水池中练习活动;自律和体力同样重要;只有从不放弃的人才准备好执行真正的任务。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How long does astronaut training take?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only one afternoon.","Years of hard training.","A single week.","No training at all."]},{"q":"What does the flight simulator feel like?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Rather boring.","Cold and wet.","Completely real.","Loud and bright."]},{"q":"What do the special pools copy?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A busy market.","A hot desert.","A deep forest.","Zero gravity."]},{"q":"What is just as important as physical strength?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Self-discipline.","Good luck.","Loud music.","A fast car."]},{"q":"Who is ready for a real mission?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Those who arrive late.","Those who never give up.","Those who dislike science.","Those who refuse to train."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Eric: There must be millions of planets like ours, so it seems likely.
Sophie: But we have found no clear evidence of it at all.
Eric: That''s true. Some scientists call this puzzle the Fermi Paradox.
Sophie: If life exists, do you think it would look like us?
Eric: Maybe, maybe not. Evolution might take a very different path.
Sophie: I really hope we make contact one day.
Eric: So do I, but the distances in space are simply enormous.', '苏菲问埃里克是否相信外星有生命;埃里克说一定有数百万颗像地球的行星,所以似乎很可能;可苏菲说至今没有确凿证据;埃里克说这个谜被称作费米悖论;苏菲问外星生命会不会像人类;埃里克说也许像也许不像,进化可能走完全不同的路;两人都希望有朝一日能联系上,但太空距离实在太遥远。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Eric think life is likely?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He has seen aliens himself.","A book told him so.","There must be millions of planets like ours.","There is only one planet."]},{"q":"What have they found no clear evidence of?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Water on the Moon.","New stars in the sky.","Rockets near Saturn.","Life on other planets."]},{"q":"What do some scientists call this puzzle?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The Fermi Paradox.","The Milky Way.","The naked eye.","The lunar landing."]},{"q":"Why might alien life look different from us?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The weather is hotter.","Evolution might take a different path.","They eat different food.","They are much older."]},{"q":"What does Eric say makes contact hard?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The lack of telescopes.","The cost of food.","The enormous distances in space.","The noise of rockets."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Real courage does not mean feeling no fear at all.
It means doing the right thing even when you are afraid.
The early astronauts knew the danger, yet they still climbed aboard.
Whenever you face a challenge, take a deep breath and keep going.', '关于探索未知,有一点值得记住:真正的勇气并不是毫无恐惧;而是即使害怕也去做对的事;早期的宇航员明知危险,却仍然登上飞船;每当你面对挑战,深吸一口气,继续前行。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does real courage not mean?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Working very hard.","Helping your friends.","Reading many books.","Feeling no fear at all."]},{"q":"What does courage really mean?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Doing the right thing even when afraid.","Running away from danger.","Never trying anything new.","Waiting for others to act."]},{"q":"What did the early astronauts know?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The price of their suits.","The danger of their journey.","The names of all stars.","The way back home only."]},{"q":"What did they do despite the danger?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They stayed at home.","They cancelled the flight.","They still climbed aboard.","They sold their rocket."]},{"q":"What should you do when you face a challenge?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Give up at once.","Forget about it.","Blame other people.","Take a deep breath and keep going."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U6', 'fltrp');

